        "id": "ch17_7_7-1",
        "text": "Exception Handling\nException/error handling will make sure to catch an error when it happens. The\nfollowing pattern must be used when you want to use error handling:\ntry:\n#Your code goes here\nexcept [Exception Object Type] as [variable]:\n#Here, you handle the exception\nfinally:\n#Add some logic to execute at the end\nWe used the exception object ( Exception as err ) in the previous example\n( write_file function). Still, there are many more exception object types (note\nthat you can just use the except keyword without the exception object type\ndeclaration, as we did in the open and read file example). As a penetration tester,\nyou will be using the exception object type most of the time. The exception object\nis the root class that handles all the types of exceptions (errors).",
